        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nI can reproduce. This is because 'mini.cmdline' assumes here that arguments of `:buffer` command must come from a fixed set of values. While that is true, the problem is that this set of values is not the same as it assumes (`vim.fn.getcompletion('', 'buffer')`, i.e. what completion must suggest, which only includes listed buffers).\n\nAlthough including unlisted buffers (both names and indexes) is doable, there is also this caveat (from `:h :buffer`): \"... A partial name also works, so long as it is unique in the list of buffers.\".\n\nSo I think it might be reasonable to disable autocorrection for this type. I'll take a closer look (soon-ish), maybe there is a better way to handle this.",
